<section id="code-lists" class="informative">
  <h2>Code lists</h2>
The tables below show, for each property of this Application Profile that takes its values from a controlled vocabulary, the vocabulary and the expected qualification:
MUST (the value space is closed under the vocabulary), RECOMMENDED (a strong preference, other values are tolerated) or MAY (a hint, other values are accepted).
The code lists defined by this Application Profile follow the tables, in alphabetical order. Their URIs are proposals under the it6 namespace.
The Source column of each code list gives the specification in which the value is defined; it is empty when the value is defined by this Application Profile.

<h3>Properties with controlled vocabularies that MUST be used</h3>
<table class="simple">
  <thead><tr><th>Property URI</th><th>Used for Class</th><th>Vocabulary name</th><th>Usage note</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>dct:format</td><td><a href="#{{ "File" | urlencode}}">File</a></td><td><a href="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type">EU Vocabularies File Type Named Authority List</a></td><td></td></tr>
    <tr><td>spdx:algorithm</td><td><a href="#{{ "Checksum" | urlencode}}">Checksum</a></td><td><a href="https://spdx.org/rdf/terms/#d4e2129">Checksum algorithm members</a></td><td>The members listed are considered a controlled vocabulary of supported checksum algorithms.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

